<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:55:22 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Countries race to secure Cop31 deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/countries-race-to-secure-cop31-deal</link><description>
COP31 climate talks have overrun their schedule as countries race to agree on a new global climate deal, following criticism of an earlier draft that made no mention of fossil fuels. The EU has warned that the current proposal risks turning the summit into a “fossil fuel summit”, as negotiators work towards a revised, potentially final agreement expected later today. France 24 International affairs editor Jamie Smith-Maillet tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d4f505c-e5c2-11f1-a7da-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-140732-141202-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d4f505c-e5c2-11f1-a7da-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-140732-141202-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">727f5284-e5c2-11f1-93d1-2d28565565a7</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:52:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>New day of protests across France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/new-day-of-protests-across-france</link><description>
France faces a sixth consecutive Saturday of protests, with demonstrators taking to the streets to rally over the rising cost of living and the government's handling of weeks of social unrest ahead of next year's presidential election. France 24 journalist Antonia Kerrigan tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a541938-e5c2-11f1-8713-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-140232-140627-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a541938-e5c2-11f1-8713-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-140232-140627-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0f612588-e5c2-11f1-9973-a9111c270733</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:50:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Cargo ship runs aground off French coast</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/cargo-ship-runs-aground-off-french-coast</link><description>
A Maltese-flagged cargo ship remains stranded off the coast of south-western France after running aground. French authorities are preparing an operation to prevent the vessel from capsizing and potentially causing pollution. The ship was not carrying any cargo, and all 19 crew members were safely evacuated by helicopter. Dan Quinlan reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1aac89e8-e5a7-11f1-b43d-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-121013-121127-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1aac89e8-e5a7-11f1-b43d-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-121013-121127-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1fa1f87a-e5a7-11f1-8d44-f7fdbeae3f0c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:52:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia tests NATO’s eastern defences</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-tests-nato-s-eastern-defences</link><description>
Two Russian missiles and a suspected drone came down in Poland on Friday in what Prime Minister Donald Tusk said was likely an "intentional provocation" timed to coincide with European military exercises in the country for a possible postwar mission in Ukraine. Senior Lecturer in Conflict and Security at King's College in London, Domitilla Sagramoso, shares further insights.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cf13c10-e5a7-11f1-ab89-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-130402-131505-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cf13c10-e5a7-11f1-ab89-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-130402-131505-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">42050920-e5a7-11f1-b311-5bb9821819cc</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:50:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Thousands protest overs prices, education, military spending in France and Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-protest-overs-prices-education-military-spending-in-france-and-europe</link><description>
France is bracing for a sixth consecutive Saturday of protests, with demonstrators expected to rally over the rising cost of living and the government's handling of weeks of social unrest ahead of next year's presidential election. France 24 journalist Antonia Kerrigan tells us the latest from Paris.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c489cff2-e5a7-11f1-bb16-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-131728-132120-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c489cff2-e5a7-11f1-bb16-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-131728-132120-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c9a3a5f8-e5a7-11f1-ae10-1594c164a15a</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:48:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Drone attack sets Russian cargo ship ablaze in Gulf of Finland</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland</link><description>
A Russian cargo ship caught fire after a drone strike in international waters in the Gulf of Finland on Saturday and later drifted into Finnish ⁠territorial waters, Finnish authorities said. Helsinki alerted NATO and imposed temporary restrictions in the area amid heightened tensions in the Baltic Sea.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d14e7d92-e5a1-11f1-ada4-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/Cargo-Finland.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d14e7d92-e5a1-11f1-ada4-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/Cargo-Finland.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">94f19a56-e5a5-11f1-bf66-3389c226a5ad</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:35:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d14e7d92-e5a1-11f1-ada4-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/Cargo-Finland.jpg">© Finnish police handout photo via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethiopia: Tackling period poverty and stigma</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-tackling-period-poverty-and-stigma</link><description><![CDATA[
In Ethiopia, entrepreneur Hanan Ahmed is tackling period poverty and the stigma surrounding menstruation. By producing affordable reusable sanitary pads and raising awareness in schools, she hopes to make menstrual health more accessible and help girls stay in class. Report by Awa Diouf & Guillaume Gougeon.
]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a9827a2-e5a4-11f1-8650-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-215007-215136-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a9827a2-e5a4-11f1-8650-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-215007-215136-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2f6b1c62-e5a4-11f1-9016-8169673db442</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:22:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethiopia - Eritrea: Troops mobilise along the border</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-eritrea-troops-mobilise-along-the-border</link><description>
More than 200 former Tigray People’s Liberation Front (TPLF) fighters surrendered to Ethiopia’s federal military Friday, state-affiliated media reported, amid escalating border tensions with neighboring Eritrea. France 24 correspondent Tom Canetti tells us the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70cf5590-e59c-11f1-9f1a-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-214828-214939-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70cf5590-e59c-11f1-9f1a-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261120-214828-214939-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">75c1206a-e59c-11f1-b8f2-ef797d14467e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:19:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Music strikes a chord at French protest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/music-strikes-a-chord-at-french-protest</link><description>
Throughout history, protest songs have brought people together across genres, rallying against war, racism, inequality and the establishment. Music is also playing a key role in the youth-led demonstrations here in France. Our reporters went to meet some of the musicians using their voices to express the protesters’ demands.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/914fa248-e592-11f1-844d-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-100844-101113-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/914fa248-e592-11f1-844d-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-100844-101113-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">968a2864-e592-11f1-a329-a98de4968e8a</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:17:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'Accept cookies'? Russia collects data from swaths of unknowing Swedes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-accept-cookies-russia-collected-data-swaths-unknowing-swedes</link><description>
A Russian tech firm backed by an oligarch close to President Vladimir Putin has secretly been collecting data from hundreds of thousands – possibly millions – of Swedes, a newspaper investigation found. The revelation has rattled the Nordic nation, whose proximity to Russia and unusually open public records system make it particularly vulnerable to Moscow’s hybrid war tactics.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75dade0c-e500-11f1-86bd-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP21173406344763.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75dade0c-e500-11f1-86bd-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP21173406344763.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7189bb56-e4fc-11f1-aa36-c70dad960c65</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:55:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75dade0c-e500-11f1-86bd-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP21173406344763.jpg">© Photo illustration Jenny Kane, AP  </source><dc:creator>Louise NORDSTROM</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'Unacceptable': EU chief condemns alleged Russian plot to kill US-Ukrainian citizen</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-unacceptable-eu-chief-condemns-alleged-russian-plot-to-kill-us-ukrainian-citizen</link><description>
European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen condemned an alleged Russian intelligence plot to assassinate a US-Ukrainian citizen in Denmark, vowing full solidarity with Copenhagen.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09933754-e590-11f1-bdd0-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T132245Z-1935520672-RC2OROAXK61L-RTRMADP-3-EU-BRITAIN-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09933754-e590-11f1-bdd0-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T132245Z-1935520672-RC2OROAXK61L-RTRMADP-3-EU-BRITAIN-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5900437c-e590-11f1-b067-8332edeefda7</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:32:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09933754-e590-11f1-bdd0-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T132245Z-1935520672-RC2OROAXK61L-RTRMADP-3-EU-BRITAIN-SUMMIT.jpg">© Yves Herman, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Was Vladimir Putin 'snubbed' by Xi Jinping? Viral handshake video is AI fake</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261121-was-vladimir-putin-snubbed-by-xi-jinping-viral-handshake-video-is-ai-fake</link><description>
A viral video appearing to show China's Xi Jinping "snubbing" Vladimir Putin at the APEC summit has racked up millions of views, fuelling speculation about tensions between Beijing and Moscow. But the footage is fake. FRANCE 24 traced the original video to an earlier summit, where the two leaders did shake hands. The creator, who runs a satire account, admitted to manipulating the footage using Grok Imagine, an AI tool developed by Elon Musk's xAI, as Vedika Bahl explains. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b200bec-e594-11f1-aa9a-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7ab1fae9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b200bec-e594-11f1-aa9a-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7ab1fae9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">701c5ae4-e58d-11f1-81f9-fb033d4bd19e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:16:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Denmark accuses Russia of assassination plot, expels diplomat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/denmark-accuses-russia-of-assassination-plot-expels-diplomat</link><description>
Denmark has accused Moscow of being behind a failed assassination attempt targeting a Ukrainian-American rapper in Copenhagen, further escalating tensions between Europe and Russia. In response, Danish authorities have ordered the expulsion of a Russian diplomat and announced tighter restrictions on visas for Russian tourists. Yuka Royer reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f0ff8e8-e58f-11f1-b96d-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-100430-100556-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f0ff8e8-e58f-11f1-b96d-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-100430-100556-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2406fa36-e58f-11f1-9e06-4bba5c36b921</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:51:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Houthis launch strikes on Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/houthis-launch-strikes-on-saudi-arabia</link><description>
Iran-backed Houthi rebels in Yemen continue to exchange strikes with the Saudi-led coalition. The coalition said it intercepted and destroyed three ballistic missiles fired towards Riyadh early on Saturday. It marks the second Houthi attack on the Saudi capital in recent days, following Saudi-led strikes on Houthi targets in Yemen. Yuka Royer has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/778980c6-e58e-11f1-b8cd-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-091902-092039-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/778980c6-e58e-11f1-b8cd-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-091902-092039-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7c72fb9e-e58e-11f1-a931-1d57297cb463</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:49:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russian projectiles hit Poland as NATO tensions rise</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russian-projectiles-hit-poland-as-nato-tensions-rise</link><description>
Three Russian projectiles came down in Poland on Friday, prompting NATO to condemn what it called a grave violation of Polish airspace. A suspected jet-powered drone and a missile struck separate locations near the Ukrainian border, while another missile crashed just 35 kilometres from an area where European troops are taking part in military exercises. Meanwhile, troops from eight NATO countries are conducting drills in neighbouring Lithuania. With US-led peace talks yet to make a breakthrough, tensions between Europe and Russia remain high. Peter O’Brien reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e70ff4a2-e58e-11f1-ba7b-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-100222-100408-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e70ff4a2-e58e-11f1-ba7b-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-100222-100408-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ec1f843a-e58e-11f1-8265-b1066ec195cd</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:47:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Nations League: France to face Spain in quarter-finals, England to take on Norway</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261121-nations-league-france-to-face-spain-in-quarter-finals-england-to-take-on-norway</link><description>
A chance for revenge. Beaten by Spain in the World Cup semi-finals last July, France will meet La Roja again in the Nations League quarter-finals next March.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd717224-e54c-11f1-8b74-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/ESPAGNE-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd717224-e54c-11f1-8b74-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/ESPAGNE-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef96b246-e54d-11f1-bff9-599cb46543dc</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:46:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU, UK reach reset deal after Brexit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/eu-uk-reach-reset-deal-after-brexit</link><description>
The UK and the EU signed three agreements on Friday at a summit in Brussels, marking a new effort to reset post-Brexit relations. The deals aim to reduce red tape for food exports, link emissions trading schemes and allow tens of thousands of young people to live and work more freely across the Channel. Prime Minister Andy Burnham has called Brexit an “obvious failure” to deliver on its promises and wants to deepen ties with the EU, a position criticised by veteran Brexiteer Nigel Farage, who has warned of a political backlash. Daniel Quinlan has this story.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9dec5f4-e58d-11f1-9664-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-091304-091457-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9dec5f4-e58d-11f1-9664-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-091304-091457-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bedc75f6-e58d-11f1-b084-57bea9daef2a</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:43:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Live: Demonstrators rally across France for sixth consecutive Saturday of protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261121-live-france-braces-for-fresh-protests-as-social-unrest-enters-sixth-week</link><description>
France faces a sixth consecutive Saturday of protests, with demonstrators taking to the streets to rally over the rising cost of living and the government's handling of weeks of social unrest ahead of next year's presidential election. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9682c2f0-e5aa-11f1-8719-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-21T122156Z-506982537-RC2CSOATMIMV-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9682c2f0-e5aa-11f1-8719-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-21T122156Z-506982537-RC2CSOATMIMV-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4dc732ec-e584-11f1-a95a-733a225569c9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:29:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9682c2f0-e5aa-11f1-8719-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-21T122156Z-506982537-RC2CSOATMIMV-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg">© Gonzalo Fuentes, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US Agriculture Department and FBI hit by cyberattacks, media report</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261121-us-agriculture-department-fbi-hit-by-cyberattacks-media-report</link><description>
Hackers breached systerms at the US Agriculture Department and the FBI, US media reported, amid a recent wave of major technology disruptions across the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8b6415c-e578-11f1-81f3-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24318480363864.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8b6415c-e578-11f1-81f3-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24318480363864.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ea07082-e578-11f1-a620-73af3d348163</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:01:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8b6415c-e578-11f1-81f3-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24318480363864.jpg">© Cliff Owen, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>House of Cards: America's enemies "no longer fear it, its allies no longer trust it'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-house-of-cards-america-s-enemies-no-longer-fear-it-its-allies-no-longer-trust-it</link><description>
The Economist's deputy editor Tom Standage joins us for a futuristic retrospective, taking us back to the future as we spotlight "The World Ahead 2027". We begin with the "leader of the free world", the FIFA Peace Prize recipient presiding over an America under the "Donroe Doctrine": "Its enemies no longer fear it and its allies no longer trust it in the way they did before."
